# attack-data.pin — the MITRE ATT&CK release the tag gate validates against.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. pySigma >= 1.5.0 resolves ATT&CK tags against a STIX bundle it
# downloads at check time, from a URL that points at the HEAD of mitre-attack/
# attack-stix-data — an unversioned, moving target — and it drops every object marked
# revoked or deprecated. So the same commit validated clean one run and reported 52
# invalid tags the next, with nothing in the repo having changed (#172). A check whose
# answer depends on what MITRE published this morning is not a gate.
#
# Pinning a VERSIONED bundle makes it one. MITRE's per-version files are immutable, and
# the digest below is checked on every run, so an ATT&CK release becomes a deliberate
# bump — "19.2 -> 20.0, here are the tags it invalidates" — reviewed in a PR, instead of
# a silent flip in a step nobody reads.
#
# TO BUMP: change version + sha256 together, re-run detections/check-attack-tags.sh, and
# retag whatever the new release revoked. The gate fails until both halves are done.
version	19.2
url	https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mitre-attack/attack-stix-data/master/enterprise-attack/enterprise-attack-19.2.json
sha256	dc1639caa5501d720e280cf1cbd8fbe009884a0c9b3e6e9ed9d0c25166c3d8f4
